Ron Johnson wrote:
>
> Why does sacrificing (sometimes) not mollify my God?

Monster level matters differently in different circumstances:

1) With an angry deity monsters below some level will have no effect at
all.  It takes a mean enough monster to have an effect.  If some monster
gets a feeling of inadequacy it isn't you that's inadequate it's the
monster type.  You can offer a hundred more like it with no effect.  You
can offer a hundred weaker monsters with no effect.  You need to try
meaner and meaner corpses until you do get an effect.  Chaotics have it
bad because they need extremely powerful monsters before they matter.
It's not worth offering a newt.

This is why it is very important to not anger your deity in the first
place.  The cost is so high and you may not be able to pray for a very
long time.

2) When your numerical alignment is negative the messages are about
"absolved".  Small monsters do have a small effect; big monsters do have
a big effect.  It's worth offering a newt but offer a mumak if you have
one.

3) When your prayer timeout is positive the messages are about
"hopeful".  Small monsters do have a small effect; big monsters do have
a big effect.  It's worth offering a newt bt offer a mumak if you have
one.

4) Once you see clovers the level of the monster no longer matters.  A
newt or a mumak give the same chance.  Before the clover you may want
that mumak to wade through the newts to get to the altar to kill it. 
After the clover clear out those popcorn monsters and offer them all.


